      "Title: ServiceNow Sorting and State Update Pitfalls\nDescription: Key UI behaviors and fields observed when sorting assets and updating task states.\n- The 'Show / hide filter' button is required to access the 'Add Sort' functionality.\n- Sorting fields are selected via a 'Order results by the following fields' combobox, not a direct dropdown.\n- After selecting a field like 'Asset function', pressing 'Enter' confirms the selection in the combobox.\n- The 'Run filter' button must be clicked explicitly to apply the new sort order.\n- The task state combobox uses the label 'Closed Complete' for the final state.\n- The 'Update' button is required to save changes to the task state.\n- Sorting criteria are reflected in the URL query parameter (e.g., 'ORDERBYasset_function').\n- The 'History' link provides context on the task's previous activity."
